        "content": "<p>cfallin requested <a href=\"https://github.com/orgs/bytecodealliance/teams/wasmtime-core-reviewers\">wasmtime-core-reviewers</a> for a review on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15183\">PR #15183</a>.</p>",
        "id": 638199657,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793984315
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>cfallin requested <a href=\"https://github.com/fitzgen\">fitzgen</a> for a review on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15183\">PR #15183</a>.</p>",
        "id": 638199658,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793984316
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>cfallin opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15183\">PR #15183</a> from <code>cfallin:memory-range-api</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>In order to support record/replay, we need precise information about when memory is mutated (so we can capture memory side-effects properly). Wasmtime's current APIs provide slices (immutable or mutable) over an entire memory, and the canonical idiom is then to subslice them further; something like <code>memory.data_mut(&amp;mut store)[start..end]</code>. We <em>can</em> support R/R with this but it ain't gonna be efficient: we'd have to capture the whole memory because we don't know about the subsequent sub-slice.</p>\n<p>This PR adds <code>Memory::data_range</code> and <code>Memory::data_range_mut</code> to borrow only one range of a memory (and an API alongside <code>Memory::data_and_store_mut</code> as well, with a bit more fiddly detail involving a <code>MemoryRanges</code> struct that represents the memory capability without requiring a full reborrow/rederivation of the borrowed <code>T</code> as well).</p>\n<p>This PR also updates both the component-model canonical ABI implementation, and Wiggle, to use this more precise API, so when we eventually implement R/R, we will have precise/small/efficient traces for all of WASIp{1,2,3} programs.</p>\n<p>&lt;!--<br>\nPlease make sure you include the following information:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>If this work has been discussed elsewhere, please include a link to that<br>\n  conversation. If it was discussed in an issue, just mention \"issue #...\".</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Explain why this change is needed. If the details are in an issue already,<br>\n  this can be brief.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Our development process is documented in the Wasmtime book:<br>\n<a href=\"https://docs.wasmtime.dev/contributing-development-process.html\">https://docs.wasmtime.dev/contributing-development-process.html</a></p>\n<p>Please review the Bytecode Alliance's AI tool usage policy at<br>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/governance/blob/main/AI_TOOL_POLICY.md\">https://github.com/bytecodealliance/governance/blob/main/AI_TOOL_POLICY.md</a></p>\n<p>Please ensure all communication follows the code of conduct:<br>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a><br>\n--&gt;</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 638199659,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793984316
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"thumbs up\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f44d\" role=\"img\" title=\"thumbs up\">:thumbs_up:</span> fitzgen submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15183#pullrequestreview-5805676347\">PR review</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>r=me w/ comments below addressed</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 638236707,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793993181
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> fitzgen created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15183#discussion_r4496625104\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Do we really not already have a method to go from <code>&amp;mut Store[Inner]&lt;T&gt;</code> to <code>(&amp;mut T, &amp;mut StoreOpaque)</code>?? That's surprising. Seems worth pulling out into its own method if we really don't.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 638236709,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793993182
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> fitzgen created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15183#discussion_r4496588834\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>And similar here</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 638236710,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793993182
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> fitzgen created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15183#discussion_r4496579406\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>And similar here</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 638236711,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793993182
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> fitzgen created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15183#discussion_r4496608722\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I think this method is a little misnamed, maybe <code>ranges_and_data_mut</code> or <code>data_ranges_and_store_data_mut</code>? Because we aren't giving back a whole store, just the store's <code>T</code> data. Unfortunate name clobber with \"data\" being both \"memory data\" and the \"store data\" :-/</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 638236712,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793993182
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> fitzgen created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15183#discussion_r4496633554\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>And then similar regarding <code>SliceIndex</code> here</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 638236713,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793993182
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> fitzgen created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15183#discussion_r4496575812\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Could this instead take a <a href=\"https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/std/slice/trait.SliceIndex.html\"><code>SliceIndex&lt;u8&gt;</code></a> so that <code>start..</code>, <code>..end</code>, <code>start..=end</code>, etc... all work with it?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 638236714,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793993182
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> fitzgen created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15183#discussion_r4496667926\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Can you also add a <code>#[should_panic]</code> test for using a memory from the wrong store? Just because we've had CVEs in the past for forgotten same-store/engine checks, which I don't think this could actually lead to in this case, but best to make sure it is covered.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 638236715,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793993182
    },
