    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> cfallin submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15183#pullrequestreview-5807782547\">PR review</a>.</p>",
        "id": 638270018,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1794003526
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> cfallin created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15183#discussion_r4498213935\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Unfortunately this would mean that we don't have the range for later dirty-memory tracking / record-replay -- the <code>SliceIndex</code> trait only lets us apply that abstract index to a slice, not get the start/end indices. (We could derive it by getting raw addresses and doing arithmetic but that seems kind of suboptimal)</p>\n<p>I'll leave this as-is on that basis, but happy to refine in followup if you have ideas here!</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 638270019,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1794003526
    },
